# ── Turso Cloud configuration — template ─────────────────────────────────────
# ✅ REMOTE edge SQLite database. Connect from local code with a URL + token.
#
# `DATABASE_TYPE` is the unified `turso`; `TURSO_URL` here is a `libsql://`
# cloud URL. (For local TursoDB use `.env.dev.turso` with a `file:///` URL.)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your values, e.g.:
#   cp .env.example.turso-cloud .env
#
# Then use it:
#   bun run dev:turso        # run the app against Turso Cloud
#   bun run db:migrate:turso # apply SQLite migrations to Turso Cloud
#   bun run test:turso       # run the endpoint tests against Turso Cloud
#
# One-time setup:
#   turso auth login                     # link your Turso account
#   turso db create movies-db            # create a database
#   turso db show movies-db --url        # copy the URL → TURSO_URL
#
# The DB auth token is NOT stored here: the deploy hooks mint a fresh permanent
# token and set it as the Cloudflare Worker secret on every deploy (see below).

# Unified Turso dialect. `turso-cloud` / `tursodb` are also accepted aliases.
DATABASE_TYPE=turso

# Connection URL (from `turso db show <db> --url`).
# e.g. libsql://movies-db-<org>.turso.io
TURSO_URL=libsql://REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_TURSO_URL

# ── Deploy lifecycle hook (used by `bun run deploy` → scripts/deploy.ts) ──────
#
# On every deploy the BEFORE hook rotates the Turso token and stores it as a
# Cloudflare Worker **secret** (never in `.env`): it invalidates the old group
# tokens, mints a fresh permanent one, and sets it via `wrangler secret put`.
# deploy.ts re-runs the build afterwards so wrangler.jsonc reflects the env.
#
# Requires the Turso CLI on PATH, `turso auth login`, and a logged-in Cloudflare
# session (`bun x wrangler login`).
BEFORE_DEPLOY_HOOK_SCRIPT=bun run scripts/hooks/before-deploy-turso.ts
